  "text": "CG\nЦГ\nEN\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAccessibility\nHomepage\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs\nDiplomatic missions\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nAndorra\nAndorra*\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nContact\nEmbassy of Montenegro in France\nVisa regime\nNationals of Andorra may may enter, pass through the territory of and stay in Montenegro for up to 90 days, with valid travel document, without a visa.\nNationals of Andorra may may enter, pass through the territory of and stay in Montenegro for up to 30, without visa, with a valid Identity Card issued by the competent authority of Andorra.\nDiplomatic Relations\nThe Principality of Andorra recognized Montenegro on June 16, 2006. Diplomatic relations were established on July 28, 2006.\nAmbassador of Montenegro in the Prinicpality of Andorra, based in Paris, is Ivan Ivanišević.\nAndorra diplomatically covers Montenegro from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Principality of Andorra in Andorra de la Vella.\nHomepage\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAsk the Government\nPR contacts\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYouTube\nFlickr\nePayment\neHealth\neGovernment\nеTax\neEnrollment\nCentral Register of Business Entities\nAccessibility\nSite map\nEnglish\n©Copyright 2026. Government of MontenegroOpšti uslovi korišćenjaThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and applies Googleprivacy policyandterms of serice.",
